# aarch64: which kernels own the 464 failing dav1d-test-data vectors

date: 2026-08-07
host: Apple M4 Pro (8P+4E), macOS 15.5, aarch64
base: `verify/compose` @ eb6f9ae (p2-kernels + NEON loop filter + NEON CDEF +
      tracker shard sizing), default features (`bitdepth_8,bitdepth_16`), no `asm`
tooling added here: `examples/md5_inventory`, `src/ablate.rs` +
      `examples/md5_ablate`, `src::safe_simd::mc_arm::compound_parity`
name sets: `benchmarks/aarch64_md5_attribution_2026-08-07/`

This is an attribution pass. Nothing was fixed.

---

## 0. TL;DR

Every one of the 464 failures is caused by an aarch64 SIMD kernel, and by
**three** of them. The partition is exact and was measured, not inferred:

| needs fixed                    | vectors | where                                        |
|--------------------------------|--------:|----------------------------------------------|
| `mc_other` alone               |      80 | 8-bit/data 79, 8-bit/issues 1                |
| `itx` alone                    |      57 | 8-bit quantizer 26, data 20, size 8, +3      |
| `itx` **and** `mc_other`       |     236 | 8-bit, incl. all 18 vq_suite                 |
| `mc_prep` **and** `mc_other`   |      91 | 10-bit/data 45, 10-bit/issues 1, 12-bit 45   |
| **total**                      | **464** |                                              |

Cumulative repair if you fix in this order: `mc_other` → 80, `+itx` → 373,
`+mc_prep` → 464. **`mc_other` is on the critical path for 407 of the 464** and
is the family with **no differential harness of any kind**.

Not guilty, measured: `mc_put`, `cdef`, `loopfilter`, `looprestoration`,
`filmgrain`, `ipred` — each breaks **zero** vectors on its own, and ablating each
repairs zero.

---

## 1. The prior attribution was wrong in both directions

The standing note was "16bpc itx and mc". Measured:

* **itx cannot be a 16bpc bug.** Every arm of
  `safe_simd::itx_arm::itxfm_add_dispatch` is gated `BD::BPC == BPC::BPC8`
  (13 arms: 4x4, 8x8, 16x16, 32x32, 8x32, 32x8, 16x32, 32x16, 64x64, 64x32,
  32x64, 16x64, 64x16). The `BPC16` branch in that file is under
  `#[cfg(feature = "asm")]`, so it is not in this build. itx breaks 293
  vectors and **all 293 are 8-bit**; it breaks 0 at 10 or 12 bits, because no
  16bpc transform runs a NEON kernel at all. The in-file comment already says
  the 16bpc kernels are "NOT bit-exact, so wiring them here would ship wrong
  pixels" — that is a latent hazard, not a current cause.
* **8-bit is the majority, not the tail.** 304 of the 358 8-bit/data vectors
  fail. A 16bpc-only hypothesis can explain at most the 91 10/12-bit failures.
* **`ipred` has no NEON in this build at all.** `intra_pred_dispatch` is
  `#[cfg(all(feature = "asm", target_arch = "aarch64"))]`, as is its call site
  in `src/ipred.rs`. Intra prediction is 100% scalar here.

Correct at HEAD: **MC_PREP 91 vectors** (the note's number is exact — 10-bit/data
45, 10-bit/issues 1, 12-bit/data 45). Stale: **ITX 103** — it is 293 now.

---

## 2. Method

### 2a. Baseline, by name

`examples/md5_inventory` writes one TSV row per vector. 766 decoded, 302 PASS,
**464 MISMATCH**, 0 ERROR, 2 skipped (non-IVF). This reproduces
`tests/decode_md5_verify`'s count exactly and, unlike it, leaves an artifact you
can set-diff: `.../md5_baseline_766.tsv.zst`, `.../failing_464.txt`.

Per group: 8-bit/data 304/358, 8-bit/quantizer 26/64, 8-bit/vq_suite 18/18,
8-bit/size 8/100, 8-bit/features 6/10, 8-bit/issues 5/15, 8-bit/{cdfupdate,
film_grain, mfmv, mv} 1 each, 8-bit/resize 2/2, 10-bit/data 45/71,
10-bit/issues 1/1, 12-bit/data 45/46. Clean: 10-bit/quantizer 64/64,
10-bit/film_grain, 8-bit/intra, 12-bit/features.

### 2b. Ablation — the causal instrument

`CpuLevel::Scalar` / `rav1d_set_cpu_flags_mask(0)` **does not disable safe SIMD
on aarch64.** Nothing under `src/safe_simd/` reads the cpu-flags mask; every
dispatcher gates on `archmage::Arm64::summon()`, which cannot fail on real
hardware. So `tests/decode_cpu_levels` compares three identical decoders here,
and any claim of the shape "it fails at all three CPU levels, therefore it is
not SIMD" is unsupported on this target. (`benchmarks/neon_tier_isolation_
2026-07-28.meta` draws exactly that conclusion for the 13 vq_suite vectors. It
is wrong: all 18 vq_suite failures are `itx` + `mc_other`, and every one passes
with SIMD ablated.)

`src/ablate.rs` adds the missing switch: a process-global bitmask of disabled
families, checked at every aarch64 `*_dispatch` entry (26 guard sites), where a
disabled family returns "not handled" and the caller runs the generic scalar
reference. Two arm shapes:

* `<family>` — that family scalar, rest NEON. Flipping to PASS ⇒ that family is
  the *only* cause (**necessary**).
* `only_<family>` — that family NEON, rest scalar. Still MISMATCH ⇒ that family
  breaks the vector *by itself* (**sufficient**). This is what disambiguates a
  vector two kernels each corrupt; such a vector is invisible in the first shape.

| arm                | MISMATCH / 464 | reading                                   |
|--------------------|---------------:|-------------------------------------------|
| `none` (baseline)  |            464 | reproduces the inventory exactly           |
| `itx`              |            407 | repairs 57                                 |
| `mc_put`           |            464 | repairs 0                                  |
| `mc_prep`          |            464 | repairs 0                                  |
| `mc_other`         |            384 | repairs 80                                 |
| `cdef`             |            464 | repairs 0                                  |
| `loopfilter`       |            464 | repairs 0                                  |
| `looprestoration`  |            464 | repairs 0                                  |
| `ipred`            |            464 | repairs 0 (no NEON ipred in this build)    |
| `filmgrain`        |            464 | repairs 0                                  |
| **`all`**          |          **0** | **all 766 pass with every kernel scalar**  |
| `only_itx`         |            293 | itx alone breaks 293                       |
| `only_mc_put`      |              0 |                                            |
| `only_mc_prep`     |             91 | mc_prep alone breaks 91                    |
| `only_mc_other`    |            407 | mc_other alone breaks 407                  |
| `only_cdef`        |              0 |                                            |
| `only_loopfilter`  |              0 |                                            |
| `only_looprestoration` |          0 |                                            |
| `only_ipred`       |              0 |                                            |
| `only_filmgrain`   |              0 |                                            |

`all` = 766/766 PASS is the load-bearing line: **the generic scalar reference is
fully conformant with dav1d on this corpus**, so it is a sound oracle, and 100%
of the failures are SIMD. Nothing is a parser, MSAC, or operating-point bug.

Set arithmetic over the `only_` arms (`itx ∪ mc_prep ∪ mc_other` = 464 exactly;
`itx ∩ mc_prep` = ∅, which is the bit-depth split falling out of the data):

```
itx only            57
mc_other only       80
itx + mc_other     236
mc_prep + mc_other  91
```

### 2c. `__simd_test_log` — one decode, cross-module mismatch census

A full-corpus decode with `--features __simd_test_log`, with a `VECTOR` marker on
stderr before each vector so per-call lines attribute (sound: `Settings::threads`
defaults to 1). 766 vectors:

| class              |    calls | vectors | groups                                   |
|--------------------|---------:|--------:|------------------------------------------|
| `ITX_MISMATCH`     |    7,855 |     293 | 8-bit only                                |
| `MC_PREP_MISMATCH` |  132,144 |      91 | 10-bit/data 45, 10-bit/issues 1, 12-bit 45|
| *(nothing logged)* |        — |      80 | 8-bit/data 79, 8-bit/issues 1             |

Zero `MC_PUT_MISMATCH`, `CDEF_MISMATCH`, `CDEF_DIR_MISMATCH`, `LF_MISMATCH`,
`LR_MISMATCH`. Zero MD5-passing vectors logged any mismatch, so on this corpus a
logged divergence always reaches the output.

The logged sets agree with the ablation sets exactly: the 80 silent vectors are
precisely the 80 that `--ablate mc_other` repairs.

ITX cells, all 8bpc: **16x16 type=11 (H_DCT) 7,190 calls / 243 vectors**;
16x32 type=9 (IDTX) 142/51; 32x16 type=9 (IDTX) 78/47; 16x32 type=0 (DCT_DCT)
16/13. This is still the `CONTEXT-HANDOFF.md` §3 list, plus 16x32 DCT_DCT.

MC_PREP: modal `max_diff` is **exactly 8192** (24,466 calls), then 8194, 2036,
8195. 8192 is `BitDepth16::PREP_BIAS`. See §4.

